%N A398132 Primes which are internal nodes in the conjectured tree of primes of sequences A398129 and A398130. Also primes in the sequence A129758.
%C A398132 According to a stronger version of Goldbach's conjecture, any prime n>3 is middle term between two other primes p and q such that p<n<q, n=p+d=q-d, or p+q=2n. Example 3<5<7 or 7<13<19.
%C A398132 Choose p and q such that d>0 is minimum. Then you may construct a rooted tree with root 3 and parent(n)=p. A few primes are not parent of any other prime, so they are the leaves of the tree, the other primes are the internal nodes, listed in this sequence.
%H A398132 Mauro Torelli, <a href="/A398129/a398129.jpg">A tree of primes</a>.
%e A398132 13 is a prime, but no prime seems to have it as a parent. So it should be a leaf in the tree, and it does not appear in the sequence.
%Y A398132 Cf. A398129, A398130.
%Y A398132 Cf. A129758: sort it and eliminate duplicates.
%K A398132 nonn,new
%O A398132 1,1
%A A398132 _Mauro Torelli_, Jul 21 2026
